title: 'pallet-broker: keep `AutoRenewals` sorted after core remapping in `renew_cores`'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `renew_cores` rebuilt `AutoRenewals` in old sale order while remapping renewed records to
    freshly allocated core indices and carrying un-renewed records over with their stale index,
    so the vector does not stay sorted by `core` once records can be carried over between sales
    (e.g. auto-renewal registered well before the renewal is due). The binary searches in
    `do_enable_auto_renew` and `do_disable_auto_renew` rely on that ordering. The rebuilt vector
    is now sorted by `core` before being written back. No live chain is affected today: no
    carried over records can currently be created, and the on-chain vectors are sorted.
crates:
- name: pallet-broker
  bump: patch
